\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If $X$ is a compact Kähler manifold with nef anticanonical class, does its universal cover decompose as

$$\widetilde X\simeq\mathbb C^q\times\prod_jY_j\times\prod_kS_k\times Z,$$

where each $Y_j$ is an irreducible Calabi–Yau manifold, each $S_k$ is an irreducible hyperkähler manifold, and $Z$ is rationally connected?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2017/39}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
If $X$ is a compact Kähler manifold with nef anticanonical class, does its universal cover decompose as

$$\widetilde X\simeq\mathbb C^q\times\prod_jY_j\times\prod_kS_k\times Z,$$

where each $Y_j$ is an irreducible Calabi–Yau manifold, each $S_k$ is an irreducible hyperkähler manifold, and $Z$ is rationally connected?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003572 (OWR-15582-006). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2017/39}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30003572}

