\section*{Universal-Cover Decomposition for Nef Anticanonical Manifolds}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Among smooth complex Fano varieties in dimension six, those with nef tangent are claimed to be rational homogeneous, with a universal-cover consequence when dimension minus maximal étale irregularity is at most six. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 067, 2026-09-25): Known contractions reduce the new case to Picard number one and pseudoindices four or five. The universal minimal-curve family has two smooth fibrations whose projection identities give linear intersection constraints; characteristic-number and integrality comparisons rule out the remaining models and identify the homogeneous possibilities.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 067, 2026-09-25): The nef-tangent uniformization corollary proves the claimed product form in its dimension-at-most-six or bounded Albanese-fiber class. The problem requires arbitrary compact Kahler manifolds with merely nef anticanonical line, not nef tangent and these dimension restrictions.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 067 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

